    <informations>Shelly Plus 1 Mini — schematic symbol.
Terminals, left to right as printed: SW O I L N.

Official sources:
https://kb.shelly.cloud/knowledge-base/shelly-plus-1-mini
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_94cd9912d38b7aa62182689cca364ff8bfb5125552b4927882fad7522224b8da/Shelly%20Plus%201%20Mini.jpg
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_48b66b938b5b1109a14a7d6431a9f6f91f81008cee5ce3ea3607433ab5c10107/Plus-1-Mini-wiring-diagram-20240528-142625.png
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_f38f730ebb74da16a5ad6166674f9b47e7716de398a75a6a95737f782d154f16/Shelly%20Plus%201%20Mini%20multilingual%20printed%20user%20and%20safety%20guide.pdf

Notes:
- Terminal order and empty center slot verified against the official front product photograph, separately from legend order.
- Rectangular Mini housing with rounded corners; front label upright and terminal strip at the top.
- No LAN connector or external CT connector.
- Potential-free relay I to O; no power measurement; SW input. Device supply is 110–240 VAC, not 12 VDC.

Open points:
- Housing radii, terminal pitch and depth details are not dimensioned CAD evidence; draw a recognizable approximation.
- Width conflict: current KB specification table says 35 mm; official printed user guide says 34 mm. The selected 34 mm width follows the printed guide; do not claim verified manufacturing precision.

Nominal dimensions and an illustrative outline: corner radii, screw pitch and recesses are drawn to be recognisable, not to manufacturing CAD.</informations>
